{"symbol":"ETE.AT","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-16T18:19:15Z","info":{"address1":"86 Eolou Street","city":"Athens","zip":"10559","country":"Greece","phone":"30 210 334 1000","website":"https://www.nbg.gr","industry":"Banks - Regional","industryKey":"banks-regional","industryDisp":"Banks - Regional","sector":"Financial Services","sectorKey":"financial-services","sectorDisp":"Financial Services","longBusinessSummary":"National Bank of Greece S.A., together with its subsidiaries, provides banking, financial products, and services primarily in Greece, Cyprus, North Macedonia, Romania, Bulgaria, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, and the United Kingdom, and internationally. It operates through Retail Banking, Corporate & Investment Banking, Trouble Assets Units, Global Markets and Asset Management, International Banking Operations, and other segments. The Retail Banking segment provides deposit, investment, bancassurance products, mortgage loans, consumer and small business lending, debit and credit cards, prepaid cards, and other traditional products and services for individual customers, professionals, and small-medium and small sized companies through its network of branches and digital businesses. Its Corporate & Investment Banking segment offers financial and investment advisory services, deposit accounts, loans, foreign exchange, and trade services for corporate customers; and lending services for large and medium-sized companies, as well as shipping finance services. The Trouble Assets Unit segment manages various non-performing and denounced loans. Its Global Markets and Asset Management segment is involved in treasury activities; and asset management, custody, private equity, and brokerage services. The International Banking Operations segment offers traditional commercial banking, such as commercial and retail credit, trade financing, foreign exchange, and deposits; shipping finance; investment banking; and brokerage services. Its Other segment engages in the real estate management and warehousing businesses. It also provides factoring, capital markets, mutual fund management, and insurance brokerage services. National Bank of Greece S.A. was founded in 1841 and is headquartered in Athens, Greece.","fullTimeEmployees":7877,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Pavlos Konstantinos Mylonas Ph.D.","age":67,"title":"CEO & Executive Director","yearBorn":1958,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1883772,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Christina T. Theofilidi","age":58,"title":"Executive Director & GM of Retail Banking","yearBorn":1967,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":1106717,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Christos D. Christodoulou","age":49,"title":"GM & Group CFO","yearBorn":1976,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Stratos  Molyviatis","age":55,"title":"GM & Group COO","yearBorn":1970,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Vasilis  Karamouzis","age":48,"title":"General Manager of Corporate & Investment Banking","yearBorn":1977,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Eleftherios  Kororos","title":"Assistant GM & Group Chief Information Officer","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Gregory  Papagrigoris","title":"Head of IR","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Panagiotis-Ioannis A. Dasmanoglou","age":62,"title":"GM of Group Compliance & Corporate Governance and Secretary","yearBorn":1963,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Georgios  Triantafillakis","age":68,"title":"General Manager of Group Legal Services","yearBorn":1957,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Chara  Dalekou","age":55,"title":"General Manager of Group Marketing","yearBorn":1970,"fiscalYear"